: null, "poll_sd": null, "poll_weight": 0.0, "fundamentals": {"margin": 16.09, "lean": 5.0, "environment": 8.2, "incumbency": 2.0, "money": 0.89}, "rating_margin": 12.89, "sigma_race": 6.8, "sigma_total": 7.55, "baseline_margin": 14.17, "analyst_adjustment": -0.67, "key_factors": ["Costa's incumbency in a district leaning Democratic by five points", "Overwhelming money edge: $939K cash on hand vs. Kirkland's $18K", "Raters split between Safe and Likely D; markets price Democrats near 94%", "No public general-election polling available"], "rationale": "Costa pairs a modest district lean with long incumbency and a dominant financial position, while Kirkland's campaign shows almost no cash on hand. Expert ratings and prediction markets both point to a comfortable Democratic win, so the fundamentals-based expectation of a low-double-digit margin stands.", "watch": "A late infusion of outside money for Kirkland or a sharply favorable Republican national environment could narrow the margin.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Jim Costa (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Jim Costa, the Democratic incumbent in this Central Valley district, enters the general election with clear advantages. The seat leans Democratic by about five points, and Costa has raised roughly $1.3 million with nearly $940,000 on hand. Republican Kyle Kirkland has raised about $339,000 but reports under $20,000 in cash, and outside spending on either side has been negligible.\n\nNo public general-election polls are available, so the picture rests on district fundamentals, campaign finance, and outside assessments. Raters split between Safe and Likely Democratic, and prediction markets put Democratic odds near 94 percent. Costa has a long record of winning re-election by double digits, and Kirkland has not shown the resources to change that dynamic. The forecast expects a comfortable Democratic victory, with the exact margin dependent on turnout in a low-information race.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9799, "margin": 14.05}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9726, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9754, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9684, "margin": 13.5}]}